From: Thibaud Michaud <thibaudm@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:26:16 +0200
Subject: Lower default stack size on Android

On 64-bit Android, Bionic's default pthread stack size
(PTHREAD_STACK_SIZE_DEFAULT) is 992 KB (1 MB minus 32 KB for
SIGNAL_STACK_SIZE_WITHOUT_GUARD) rather than 1 MB.

Lower V8_DEFAULT_STACK_SIZE_KB on 64-bit Android to 952 KB (and 928 KB
under ASan) to preserve the 40 KB (resp. 64 KB) stack limit safety
margin.

Bug: 568908052
Change-Id: Id403fdd5f266d2574acead1b29aa7e7026d5e76c
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8579382
Commit-Queue: Thibaud Michaud <thibaudm@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Jakob Kummerow <jkummerow@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#110794}
Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
This branch's globals.h has no V8_STACK_LIMIT_MARGIN_KB macro (introduced
upstream after M150), so the two "#define V8_STACK_LIMIT_MARGIN_KB" lines
of the upstream diff (64 in the ASan branch, 40 in the new Android branch)
are not carried. The V8_DEFAULT_STACK_SIZE_KB changes (928 for ASan on
Android, 952 for 64-bit Android) are applied unchanged.

diff --git a/src/common/globals.h b/src/common/globals.h
index d922c9149935bf99e24a7804d8c3746994e5acd7..82bdbca8524323f40f837691a4a276dfe0210744 100644
--- a/src/common/globals.h
+++ b/src/common/globals.h
@@ -191,7 +191,17 @@ namespace internal {
 // even just 1 KB less than the default stack size would be enough (see
 // crbug.com/1486275); to be more robust towards future CF reports we'll
 // use an even lower limit.
+#if V8_OS_ANDROID
+#define V8_DEFAULT_STACK_SIZE_KB 928
+#else
 #define V8_DEFAULT_STACK_SIZE_KB 960
+#endif
+#elif V8_OS_ANDROID
+// On 64-bit Android, Bionic's default pthread stack size
+// (PTHREAD_STACK_SIZE_DEFAULT) is 992 KB (1 MB minus 32 KB for
+// SIGNAL_STACK_SIZE_WITHOUT_GUARD). Leave the same 40 KB margin as on
+// 1 MB stack systems.
+#define V8_DEFAULT_STACK_SIZE_KB 952
 #else
 // Slightly less than 1MB, since Windows' default stack size for
 // the main execution thread is 1MB.
